# Cloudflare Pages headers (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/)
#
# Framing policy — scoped to the embed route ONLY.
#
# Every other path is intentionally left untouched here so its current
# header behaviour is unchanged. Only /embed/* is made iframe-able so other
# sites (blogs, course material) can embed the visualiser like a YouTube video.
#
# `frame-ancestors *` allows any site to frame /embed/*. To restrict it to a
# specific allow-list instead, replace `*` with space-separated origins, e.g.
#   Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors https://yoursite.com https://*.edu
#
# NOTE: Cloudflare Pages does not send X-Frame-Options by default, so no
# removal is needed here. If an X-Frame-Options: DENY/SAMEORIGIN header is set
# elsewhere (e.g. a Cloudflare Transform Rule or the dashboard), it must be
# relaxed for /embed/* THERE — a _headers file cannot delete a header added by
# another layer.
/embed/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors *
